  "gaps": [
    "The 21-credit general education block is not printed; it is derived as 45 required general education quarter credits minus the 24 quarter credits of required math courses (MAT1050, MAT1200, MAT2051, MAT2200). This assumes those courses count toward the 45, because they are listed under General Education Requirements. Confirm this with the catalog or the school.",
    "General education requires a minimum of 4 quarter credits from each category (Communication, Humanities, Natural Science and Mathematics, Social Science). The ledger cannot verify how the remaining credits are distributed across these categories.",
    "The total of 180 quarter credits must include a minimum of 54 quarter credits from the 3000-level and above. This is a distribution constraint that is not captured as a separate requirement line.",
    "Recommended (not required) courses are not included in the ledger: HUM1350 Culture, Continuity, and Change (6) and IT3180 Pathways to Certificate-Based Professional Development (6).",
    "An optional Honors Pathway exists. PHI-H2005 (3), COM-H4005 (6) and SOC-H3005 (6), at least 15 quarter credits, apply toward general education for honors students. It is not included as a base requirement.",
    "Capstone courses must be taken during the student's final two quarters. The capture does not state whether capstone or any other courses must be completed at Capella; no residency or institutional-credit requirement is stated.",
    "Course prerequisites are referenced but not detailed in the capture.",
    "The capture also begins a FlexPath option of this program measured in program points. That capture is truncated after the general education section, so the FlexPath ledger cannot be built and is excluded here."
  ],
